handicrafts and art collections.&nbsp; Witness some cultural events and enjoy your dinner at Dilli Haat, exploring Indian cuisines. Overnight stay in Delhi.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 05:40:36','2025-11-15 05:40:36',NULL,50),(155,'{\"time\":1763185270201,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"l4SvLWdUGg\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Note:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763185270202,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"HrZtTI-Aau\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Driver passes are required at Red Fort, India Gate, Rashtrapati Bhawan, and Hawa Mahal. All monuments are open from sunrise to sunset. Chandani Chowk (Closed on Sundays). The Taj Mahal is closed on Fridays.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 05:41:10','2025-11-15 05:41:10',NULL,50),(156,'{\"time\":1763187649502,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"0awaBNBBEj\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 7:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763187649508,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"ne7WtU1gxK\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Check out from the Jaipur hotel after breakfast and enjoy a scenic drive to Delhi Airport/Railway Station.&nbsp;\"}},{\"id\":\"q6Fu6OmOdU\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"As your journey comes to an end, you return home with your heart full of devotion, your mind enriched with history, and your soul glowing with unforgettable memories of Indiaâ€™s culture and divinity.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 06:20:49','2025-11-15 06:20:49',NULL,51),(157,'{\"time\":1763187685383,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"xiRj6oLEdP\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 6:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763187685383,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"PGqAVpCmH6\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, meet your tour guide and explore the royal landmarks of the city, starting with Amber Fort located atop the Aravalli Hills. Built in 1592 by Raja Man Singh I, the fort is an architectural marvel blending Rajput and Mughal styles. Explore the mesmerizing beauty of Sheesh Mahal (Mirror Palace), Ganesh Pol, and the Diwan-i-Aam (Hall of Public Audience). The detailed mirror work and magnificent courtyards make it one of the most iconic forts of India. Now head towards City Palace, a grand complex that still serves as a residence of the royal family of Jaipur. Constructed by Maharaja Sawai Jai Singh II, the palace showcases a perfect blend of Rajput, Mughal, and European architecture. Towards the afternoon, take a quick lunch break and savor the flavors of Rajasthan. After regaining energy, move to your next location, Jantar Mantar, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Jantar Mantar is an astronomical observatory built in 1734 by Maharaja Jai Singh II, who was passionate about astronomy. The site contains 19 architectural instruments that can measure time, track celestial bodies, and predict eclipses, all with remarkable accuracy, centuries before modern equipment. &nbsp; visit the Hawa Mahal, situated in the center of the city, Jaipurâ€™s most recognizable landmark. Built in 1799 by Maharaja Sawai Pratap Singh, this five-story pink sandstone structure has 953 small windows (jharokhas) adorned with intricate lattice work. Wind up your day with some shopping and exploring the vibrant market of Jaipur and enjoying a comfortable stay.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 06:21:25','2025-11-15 06:21:25',NULL,51),(158,'{\"time\":1763187717300,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"oYwAva3nqR\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 5:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763187717301,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"iGmLQrlwax\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Experience the magic of the Taj Mahal at sunrise As the first rays of dawn kiss the white marble, the Taj Mahal awakens in a golden glow, casting its reflection across the tranquil Yamuna River. This is the most enchanting time to witness the monument. Explore the Taj Mahal. Come back to your hotel and enjoy the comforting breakfast. Check out and depart for Jaipur in your private vehicle via Fatehpur Sikri (1-hour drive). Explore Fatehpur Sikri. Take a break for lunch and then visit Fatehpur Sikri, a UNESCO World Heritage Site built by Emperor Akbar in the 16th century. It was the capital of the Mughal Empire, built with red sandstone, and it is an architectural masterpiece that blends Persian, Indian, and Islamic styles. Walking through Fatehpur Sikri feels like stepping back in time, with its well-preserved palaces, courtyards, and gateways narrating stories of the Mughal eraâ€™s grandeur and vision. Take a lunch break to boost your energy, and then depart for Jaipur (3-4 hours drive). Check in at your stay in Jaipur, and then in the evening head for a cultural retreat and authentic Rajasthani dinner at Chokhi Dhani village. Enjoy the folk dance and music, camel rides, and wind up your day with a Rajasthani cultural dinner. Drive back to the hotel and enjoy your comfortable stay.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 06:21:57','2025-11-15 06:21:57',NULL,51),(159,'{\"time\":1763187752514,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"Xn2qQxbr8B\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 4:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763187752515,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"Gwz6YPDsh8\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast depart to Agra with your private&nbsp; (2-hour drive) check in at your Agra hotel and then continue your exploration retreat visit the Agra Fort, standing on the banks of River Yamuna, Agra Fort is also one the most magnificent Mughal monuments and a UNESCOâ€™s World Heritage site. Built in 1565 AD by the great Mughal emperor&nbsp; &nbsp;( ahead in this timeless journey visit the exquisite charming Baby Taj (Itmad-uh- Daulah) built in 1622 &amp; 1628 its also a white marble beauty commissioned by Empress Nur Jahan wife of Emperor Jahangir in the memory of her beloved father Mirza Ghiyas Beg. Afterwards explore Agraâ€™s local market and enjoy Agra\'s famous â€œPethaâ€ and wind up your day with a comfortable stay in Agra.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 06:22:32','2025-11-15 06:22:32',NULL,51),(160,'{\"time\":1763187780068,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"hRoe7rEf_X\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 3:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763187780068,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"1zCXBYB-5R\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, head towards your private vehicle as your much-awaited journey begins. Depart from Delhi and take a scenic drive to Mathura Vrindavan (2-3 hrs drive). Upon arrival, check into the hotel and head towards your spiritual yatra to the exact spot where Lord Krishna was born over 5000 years ago, â€œShri Krishna Janmabhoomi Temple.â€ This temple holds immense faith amongst all the devotees worldwide and is one of the most sacred shrines. Next, visit the Dwarkadhish Temple, built in 1814 by a devotee named Seth Gokul Das Parikh. The temple has beautiful Rajasthani-style architecture and detailed carvings; its beauty will leave you mesmerized. Take your lunch break by savoring the traditional vegetarian meal in local restaurants of Mathura. Going ahead visit the famous Banke Bihari Temple and ISKCON Temple, and Lastly visit the Prem Mandir witness the beautiful temple in the evening as it was illuminated with colorful lights, creating a visually magical experience. Enjoy your evening at your comfortable overnight stay in Mathura Vrindavan.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 06:23:00','2025-11-15 06:23:00',NULL,51),(161,'{\"time\":1763187805654,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"2f9_11lUA1\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 2:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763187805654,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"t2KfgGA-sH\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, head towards your private vehicle and begin your journey, stepping back in time as you enter the beauty and chaos of Old Delhi. Explore the narrow streets of Chandni Chowk with a ride and visit all the famous chaotic lanes like â€œParathe Wali Gali,â€ experience a guided food walk tour, and savor the authentic flavors that define Delhiâ€™s culinary soul. Explore Jalebi Wala, Karimâ€™s, Al Jawahar, and Natraj Dahi Bhalla, and indulge as much as your heart (and stomach) can hold. Visit the Red Fort in Purani Dilli. Also, you can shop for beautiful Indian outfits and artifacts if time allows.&nbsp; Visit India Gate (the iconic war memorial dedicated to Indian soldiers) and Rashtrapati Bhavan (the majestic Presidential Residence outside view). Continue exploration where modernity blends with Mughal and colonial history by visiting Humayun\'s Tomb (the architectural inspiration behind the Taj Mahal). Qutub Minar (the worldâ€™s tallest brick minar, a UNESCO World Heritage site).&nbsp; As the day winds up, enjoy a comfortable stay at the hotel.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 06:23:25','2025-11-15 06:23:25',NULL,51),(162,'{\"time\":1763187830578,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"GuprZgGpEu\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 1:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763187830578,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"V_FDKzICFB\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Arrive in Delhi, meet TrippyJiffy\'s representative, and check in to your comfortable stay. Relax and enjoy the property. In the afternoon at 16:00 hrs depart for Dilli Haat, Delhi\'s iconic vibrant market filled with numerous options of Indian handicrafts and art collections.&nbsp; Witness some cultural events and enjoy your dinner at Dilli Hatt, exploring Indian cuisines. Overnight stay in Delhi.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 06:23:50','2025-11-15 06:23:50',NULL,51),(163,'{\"time\":1763187865066,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"4A1YooNkeu\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Note:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763187865067,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"rtcg0UpnDU\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Driver passes are required at Red Fort, India Gate, Rashtrapati Bhawan, and Hawa Mahal. All monuments are open from sunrise to sunset. Chandani Chowk (Closed on Sundays). The Taj Mahal is closed on Fridays.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 06:24:25','2025-11-15 06:24:25',NULL,51),(164,'{\"time\":1763189245275,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"DJ5BYiUms1\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 9:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763189245275,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"oYLFJm_rCA\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Wake up early in the morning to witness the breathtaking beauty of the royal magnificence of the Taj Mahal, a monument so captivating that you won\'t be able to take your eyes off it. At sunrise, as the first rays of dawn kiss the white marble, the Taj Mahal awakens in a golden glow, casting its reflection across the tranquil Yamuna River. This is the most enchanting time to witness the monument. Explore the Taj Mahal. Come back to your hotel and enjoy the comforting breakfast. After breakfast, check out of the hotel and start your exploration of a beautiful monument holding Indiaâ€™s ancient history that awaits you: â€œThe Agra Fort.â€ Standing on the banks of the River Yamuna, Agra Fort is also one of the most magnificent Mughal monuments and a UNESCO World Heritage site. Built in 1565 AD by the great Mughal emperor Akbar, the fort is made of red sandstone. Agra Fort stands as a symbol of architectural brilliance and a silent witness of centuries of Indiaâ€™s royal history, power, and love. Pause for a moment, take a lunch break to refresh yourself and boost your energy, and then head back to Delhi Airport as you return in spirit and enriched with timeless memories of Indiaâ€™s culture, spirituality, and heritage.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 06:47:25','2025-11-15 06:47:25',NULL,52),(165,'{\"time\":1763189270863,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"8mQloY5i3z\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 8:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763189270863,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"UYDEeYxmlW\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Check out from the Jaipur hotel after breakfast and enjoy a scenic drive to Agra (approx. 4-5 hrs. drive) via Fatehpur Sikri. Take a break for lunch and then visit Fatehpur Sikri, a UNESCO World Heritage Site built by Emperor Akbar in the 16th century. It was the capital of the Mughal Empire, built with red sandstone, and it is an architectural masterpiece that blends Persian, Indian, and Islamic styles. Walking through Fatehpur Sikri feels like stepping back in time, with its well-preserved palaces, courtyards, and gateways narrating stories of the Mughal eraâ€™s grandeur and vision. Depart for Agra and check in to your hotel and enjoy a comfortable overnight stay.&nbsp;\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 06:47:50','2025-11-15 06:47:50',NULL,52),(166,'{\"time\":1763189327795,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"cr7C2q-UO9\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 7:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763189327795,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"ISorT-DXtL\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, meet your tour guide and explore the royal landmarks of the city, starting with Amber Fort located atop the Aravalli Hills. Built in 1592 by Raja Man Singh I, the fort is an architectural marvel blending Rajput and Mughal styles. Explore the mesmerizing beauty of Sheesh Mahal (Mirror Palace), Ganesh Pol, and the Diwan-i-Aam (Hall of Public Audience). The detailed mirror work and magnificent courtyards make it one of the most iconic forts of India. Now head towards City Palace, a grand complex that still serves as a residence of the royal family of Jaipur. Constructed by Maharaja Sawai Jai Singh II, the palace showcases a perfect blend of Rajput, Mughal, and European architecture. Towards the afternoon, take a quick lunch break and savor the flavors of Rajasthan. After regaining energy, move to your next location, Jantar Mantar, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Jantar Mantar is an astronomical observatory built in 1734 by Maharaja Jai Singh II, who was passionate about astronomy. The site contains 19 architectural instruments that can measure time, track celestial bodies, and predict eclipses, all with remarkable accuracy, centuries before modern equipment. Lastly, visit the Hawa Mahal, situated in the center of the city, Jaipurâ€™s most recognizable landmark. Built in 1799 by Maharaja Sawai Pratap Singh, this five-story pink sandstone structure has 953 small windows (jharokhas) adorned with intricate lattice work. Wind up your day with some shopping and exploring the vibrant market of Jaipur and enjoying a comfortable stay.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 06:48:48','2025-11-15 06:48:48',NULL,52),(167,'{\"time\":1763189364985,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"G_7K_bG6Qz\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 6:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763189364985,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"bAp5H1hEO5\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, check out of Delhi hotel and board your private vehicle as your much-awaited journey begins. depart from Delhi and take a scenic drive to Jaipur (approx. 5-6 hrs. drive). Reach Jaipur, the Pink City, by afternoon and check in to the hotel and relax after your journey. In the evening, visit the local market of Jaipur and then head towards Chokhi Dhani, where you enjoy the folk dance and music, camel rides, and wind up your day with a Rajasthani cultural dinner. Drive back to the hotel and enjoy your comfortable stay.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 06:49:25','2025-11-15 06:49:25',NULL,52),(168,'{\"time\":1763189456019,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"4z33jKdvev\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 5:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763189456019,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"Vqt_DYOYoT\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, check out of the Rishikesh hotel and start your drive to Delhi (5-6 hours). Reach Delhi, check in at the hotel, and enjoy a comfortable overnight stay. Relax and regain your energy for the second leg of your journey.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 06:50:56','2025-11-15 06:50:56',NULL,52),(169,'{\"time\":1763189497472,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"qZ3uV0mypw\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 4:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763189497472,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"jLI3OHEJD1\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, check out from the Haridwar hotel and depart for Rishikesh, the world-renowned Yoga Capital situated on the serene banks of the Ganges and surrounded by the Himalayas. Visit the famous Lakshman Jhula &amp; Ram Jhula bridges over the River Ganges as per our Hindu mythology, Lord Lakshman, and the River Ganga using jute rope. Experience the soul-stirring experience by visiting Triveni Ghat for Ganga Aarti. Enjoy your comfortable stay at Rishikesh.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 06:51:37','2025-11-15 06:51:37',NULL,52),(170,'{\"time\":1763189547564,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"nQCEOc_p30\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 3:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763189547564,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"GXrp3fAg1m\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, head towards your private vehicle as your much-awaited journey begins. Depart from Delhi and take a scenic drive to Haridwar &amp; Rishikesh, surrounded by the beautiful Himalayas. Peace awaits you. Enjoy a comfortable drive to Haridwar (approx. 5-6 hrs). Check in at the hotel to explore Haridwarâ€™s timeless charm and explore vibrant markets, holy ghats, and temples. Visit Mansa Devi Temple located on Bilwat Parvat Hill; this temple is dedicated to Goddess Mansa Devi. Later visit Shanti Kunj, Sapt Rishi Dhara, and Bharat Mata Temple. In the evening, enjoy the famous Ganga Aarti at Har Ki Paudi and take a dip in the divine waters of River Ganga. Later enjoy a traditional vegetarian dinner at a local restaurant and enjoy a comfortable stay at Haridwar.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 06:52:28','2025-11-15 06:52:28',NULL,52),(171,'{\"time\":1763189587488,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"WRKxVWsqnQ\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 2:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763189587488,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"HRvRQ9LXEG\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, head towards your private vehicle and begin your journey, stepping back in time as you enter the beauty and chaos of Old Delhi. Explore the narrow streets of Chandni Chowk with a rickshaw ride and visit all the famous chaotic lanes like â€œParathe Wali Gali.â€ Experience a guided food walk tour and savor authentic flavors that define Delhiâ€™s culinary soul. Explore Jalebi Wala, Karimâ€™s, Al Jawahar, and Natraj Dahi and indulge as much as your heart (and stomach) can hold. Visit the Red Fort in Purani Dilli. You can shop for beautiful Indian outfits and artifacts if time allows.&nbsp; Visit India Gate (the iconic war memorial dedicated to Indian soldiers) and Rashtrapati Bhavan (the majestic Presidential Residence outside view). Continue exploration where modernity blends with Mughal and colonial history by visiting Tomb (the architectural inspiration behind the Taj Mahal). Qutub Minar (the worldâ€™s tallest brick minar, a UNESCO World Heritage site).&nbsp; As the day winds up, enjoy a comfortable stay at the hotel.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 06:53:07','2025-11-15 06:53:07',NULL,52),(172,'{\"time\":1763189621542,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"Y3pOW1CfQb\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 1:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763189621542,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"wmmxT5pdMc\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Arrive in Delhi, meet TrippyJiffy\'s representative, and check in to your comfortable stay. Relax and enjoy the property. In the afternoon at 16:00 hrs depart for Dilli Haat, Delhi\'s iconic vibrant market filled with numerous options of Indian handicrafts and art collections.&nbsp; Witness some cultural events and enjoy your dinner at Dilli Haat, exploring Indian cuisines. Overnight stay in Delhi.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 06:53:41','2025-11-15 06:53:41',NULL,52),(173,'{\"time\":1763190091610,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"ETOmV6gMjR\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 7:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763190091610,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"IQwXvMeTjZ\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Wake up early in the morning to witness the breathtaking beauty of the royal magnificence of the Taj Mahal, a monument so captivating that you won\'t be able to take your eyes off it. At sunrise, as the first rays of dawn kiss the white marble, the Taj Mahal awakens in a golden glow, casting its reflection across the tranquil Yamuna River. This is the most enchanting time to witness the monument. Explore the Taj Mahal. Come back to your hotel and enjoy the comforting breakfast. After breakfast, check out of the hotel and start your exploration of a beautiful monument holding Indiaâ€™s ancient history that awaits: â€œThe Agra Fort.â€ Standing on the banks of the River Yamuna, Agra Fort is also one of the most magnificent Mughal monuments and a UNESCO World Heritage site. Built in 1565 AD by the great Mughal emperor Akbar, the fort is made of red sandstone. Agra Fort stands as a symbol of architectural brilliance and a silent witness of centuries of Indiaâ€™s royal history, power, and love. Pause for a moment, take a lunch, refresh yourself, and boost your energy,, and then head back to Delhi Airport as you return in spirit and enriched with timeless memories of Indiaâ€™s heritage and the vibrant beauty of its wildlife.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 07:01:31','2025-11-15 07:01:31',NULL,53),(174,'{\"time\":1763190115185,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"SZmzQH8Wpe\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 6:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763190115185,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"vYHNZbsghQ\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, start the next leg of the journey from Bharatpur to Agra via Fatehpur Sikri (1-2 hours). Visit Fatehpur, a UNESCO World Heritage Site built by Emperor Akbar in the 16th century. It was the capital of the Mughal Empire, built with red sandstone. It is an architectural masterpiece that blends Persian, Indian, and Islamic styles. Walking through Fatehpur Sikri feels like stepping back in time, with its well-preserved palaces, courtyards, and gateways narrating stories of the Mughal eraâ€™s grandeur and vision. Depart for Agra and check in to your hotel and enjoy a comfortable overnight stay.&nbsp;\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 07:01:55','2025-11-15 07:01:55',NULL,53),(175,'{\"time\":1763190143291,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"M5M-zV8l8o\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 5:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763190143291,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"fGXZJg9cm7\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Check out from the hotel after breakfast and enjoy a scenic drive to Bharatpur (3-4 hours). Check in at the hotel in Bharatpur and enjoy an evening safari of Bharatpur Bird Sanctuary (Keoladeo National Park), a UNESCO World Heritage Site home to hundreds of resident and migratory bird species. Enjoy an overnight stay at Bharatpur Bird Sanctuary.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 07:02:23','2025-11-15 07:02:23',NULL,53),(176,'{\"time\":1763190168155,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"9IfGX8pGhU\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 4:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763190168155,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"rqG_el2kbp\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, meet your tour g