nd take a scenic drive to Jaipur (approx. 5-6 hrs).&nbsp; Reach Jaipur, the Pink City, by afternoon and check in to the hotel and relax after your journey. In the evening, visit the local market of Jaipur and then head towards Chokhi Dhani, where you enjoy the folk dance and music, camel rides, and wind up your day with a Rajasthani cultural dinner. Drive back to the hotel and enjoy your comfortable stay.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 07:03:13','2025-11-15 07:03:13',NULL,53),(178,'{\"time\":1763190216747,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"pFT_BpW-0x\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 2:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763190216747,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"A2-i80sJ7q\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, head towards your private vehicle and begin your journey, stepping back in time as you enter the beauty and chaos of Old Delhi. Explore the narrow streets of Chandni Chowk with a rickshaw ride and visit all the famous chaotic lanes like â€œParathe Wali Gali.â€ Experience a guided food walk tour and savor authentic flavors that define Delhiâ€™s culinary soul. Explore Jalebi Wala, Karimâ€™s, Al Jawahar, and Natraj Dahi Bhalla, and indulge as much as your heart (and stomach) can hold. Visit the Red Fort in Purani Dilli. Also, you can shop for beautiful Indian outfits and artifacts if time allows.&nbsp; Visit India Gate (the iconic war memorial dedicated to Indian soldiers) and Rashtrapati Bhavan (the majestic Presidential Residence outside view). Continue exploration where modernity blends with Mughal and colonial history by visiting Humayun\'s Tomb (the architectural inspiration behind the Taj Mahal). Qutub Minar (the worldâ€™s tallest brick minar, a UNESCO World Heritage site).&nbsp; As the day winds up, enjoy a comfortable stay at the hotel.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 07:03:36','2025-11-15 07:03:36',NULL,53),(179,'{\"time\":1763190244817,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"p4NAivkJZ7\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 1:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763190244818,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"YFEwr24sFg\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Arrive in Delhi, meet TrippyJiffy\'s representative, and check in to your comfortable stay. Relax and enjoy the property. In the afternoon at 16:00 hrs depart for Delhi. Delhi\'s iconic vibrant market is filled with numerous options of Indian handicrafts and art collections.&nbsp; Witness some cultural events and enjoy your dinner at Dilli Hatt, exploring Indian cuisines. Overnight stay in Delhi.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 07:04:04','2025-11-15 07:04:04',NULL,53),(180,'{\"time\":1763190280426,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"yFu8-L0aW8\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Note:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763190280426,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"6gaRPqq5uU\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Driver passes are required at Red Fort, India Gate, Rashtrapati, and Hawa Mahal. All monuments are open from Sunrise to Sunset. Chandani Chowk (Closed on Sundays). Taj Mahal is closed on Fridays\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 07:04:40','2025-11-15 07:04:40',NULL,53),(181,'{\"time\":1763191018330,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"KlQFwiRtxi\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 7:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763191018330,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"nImjnrM-WH\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Wake up early in the morning to witness the breathtaking beauty of the royal magnificence of the Taj Mahal, a monument so captivating that you won\'t be able to take your eyes off it. At sunrise, as the first rays of dawn kiss the white marble, the Taj Mahal awakens in a golden glow, casting its reflection across the tranquil Yamuna River. This is the most enchanting time to witness the monument. Explore the Taj Mahal. Come back to your hotel and enjoy the comforting breakfast. After breakfast, check out of the hotel and start your exploration of a beautiful monument holding Indiaâ€™s ancient history that awaits you: â€œThe Agra Fort.â€ Standing on the banks of the River Yamuna, Agra Fort is also one of the most magnificent Mughal monuments and a UNESCO World Heritage site. Built in 1565 AD by the great Mughal emperor Akbar, the fort is made of red sandstone. Agra Fort stands as a symbol of architectural brilliance and a silent witness of centuries of Indiaâ€™s royal history, power, and love. Pause for a moment, take a lunch break to refresh yourself and boost your energy, and then head back to Delhi Airport. From majestic palaces to tiger trails, this tour ends with a treasure of memories that reflect Indiaâ€™s charm, diversity, and wild beauty.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 07:16:58','2025-11-15 07:16:58',NULL,54),(182,'{\"time\":1763191041239,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"QesjmCo4CL\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 6:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763191041240,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"AynJqZOhXd\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Early morning for another session of wilderness and serenity for an early morning safari. After the safari, enjoy a comforting breakfast and start the next leg of the journey from Ranthambore to Agra via Fatehpur Sikri (5-6 hours) Visit Fatehpur Sikri, a UNESCO World Heritage Site built by Emperor Akbar in the 16th century. It was the capital of the Mughal Empire, built with red sandstone. It is an architectural masterpiece that blends Persian, Indian, and Islamic styles. Walking through Fatehpur Sikri feels like stepping back in time, with its well-preserved palaces, courtyards, and gateways narrating stories of the Mughal eraâ€™s grandeur and vision. Depart for Agra and check in to your hotel and enjoy a comfortable overnight stay.&nbsp;\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 07:17:21','2025-11-15 07:17:21',NULL,54),(183,'{\"time\":1763191067231,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"I7WmqpcsJW\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 5:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763191067231,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"-sSxvGtFMN\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Check out from the Jaipur hotel after breakfast and enjoy a scenic drive to Ranthambore (3-4 hours). Upon arrival, check in at the hotel in Ranthambore and later head out for an exciting experience: an evening safari of Ranthambore National Park Sanctuary, known for its thriving population of Bengal tigers, a rare sight to look at. Its diverse scenic and wildlife landscape makes it one of the most unforgettable wildlife experiences.&nbsp;\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 07:17:47','2025-11-15 07:17:47',NULL,54),(184,'{\"time\":1763191094965,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"bHB_RX0RC4\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 4:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763191094965,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"AOqEHReq5-\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, meet your tour guide and explore the royal landmarks of the city, starting with Amber Fort located atop the Aravalli Hills. Built in 1592 by Raja Man Singh I, the fort is an architectural marvel blending Rajput and Mughal styles. Explore the mesmerizing beauty of Sheesh Mahal (Mirror Palace), Ganesh Pol, and the Diwan-i-Aam (Hall of Public Audience). The detailed mirror work and magnificent courtyards make it one of the most iconic forts of India. Now head towards City Palace, a grand complex that still serves as a residence of the royal family of Jaipur. Constructed by Maharaja Sawai Jai Singh II, the palace showcases a perfect blend of Rajput, Mughal, and European architecture. Towards the afternoon, take a quick lunch break and savor the flavors of Rajasthan. After regaining energy, move to your next location, Jantar Mantar, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Jantar Mantar is an astronomical observatory built in 1734 by Maharaja Jai Singh II, who was passionate about astronomy. The site contains 19 architectural instruments that can measure time, track celestial bodies, and predict eclipses, all with remarkable accuracy, centuries before modern equipment. Lastly, visit the Hawa Mahal, situated in the center of the city, Jaipurâ€™s most recognizable landmark. Built in 1799 by Maharaja Sawai Pratap Singh, this five-story pink sandstone structure has 953 small windows (jharokhas) adorned with intricate lattice work. Wind up your day with some shopping and exploring the vibrant market of Jaipur and enjoying a comfortable stay.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 07:18:15','2025-11-15 07:18:15',NULL,54),(185,'{\"time\":1763191121541,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"97T5l1ljvN\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 3:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763191121541,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"yV8LEFZ68c\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, check out of Delhi hotel and board your private vehicle as your much awaited journey begins, depart from Delhi and take a scenic drive to Jaipur (Approx 5-6 hrs drive) Reach Jaipur the Pink City by afternoon and check in to the hotel and relax after your journey. In the evening visit the local market of Jaipur and then head towards Chokhi Dhani where you enjoy the folk dance and music, camel rides and wind up your day with a Rajasthani cultural dinner. Drive back to the hotel and enjoy your comfortable stay.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 07:18:41','2025-11-15 07:18:41',NULL,54),(186,'{\"time\":1763191148135,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"wFP93GKxam\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 2:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763191148136,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"6z2Lu4L9Iy\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, head towards your private vehicle and begin your journey stepping back in time as you enter the beauty and chaos of Old Delhi explore the narrow streets of Chandni Chowk with Rickshaw ride and visiting all the famous chaotic lanes like â€œParathe Wali Galiâ€ experience a guided food walk tour, Savor the authentic flavours that define Delhiâ€™s culinary soul. Explore Jalebi Wala, Karimâ€™s, Al Jawahar, Natraj Dahi Bhalla and indulge as much as your heart (and stomach) can hold. Visit the Red Fort in Purani Dilli. Also you can shop for beautiful Indian outfits and artifacts if time allows.&nbsp; Visit India Gate (The iconic war memorial dedicated to Indian soldiers) and Rashtrapati Bhavan (The majestic Presidential Residence outside view). Continue exploration where modernity blends with Mughal and Colonial History by visiting Humayun Tomb (the architectural inspiration behind Taj Mahal).Qutub Minar (Worldâ€™s tallest brick minar, a UNESCO World Heritage site).&nbsp; As the day winds up, enjoy a comfortable stay at the hotel.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 07:19:08','2025-11-15 07:19:08',NULL,54),(187,'{\"time\":1763191171093,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"42qGsMEuBp\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 1:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763191171093,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"6jvRmdV749\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Arrive in Delhi, meet TrippyJiffy\'s representative, and check in to your comfortable stay. Relax and enjoy the property.&nbsp; In the afternoon at 16:00 hrs, depart for Dilli Haat, Delhi\'s iconic vibrant market filled with numerous options of Indian art collections.&nbsp; Witness some cultural events and enjoy your dinner at Dilli Hatt, exploring Indian cuisines. Overnight stay in Delhi.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 07:19:31','2025-11-15 07:19:31',NULL,54),(188,'{\"time\":1763191206035,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"dLNRzz8B4U\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Note:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763191206036,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"d_gKjyGI6a\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Driver passes are required at Red Fort, India Gate, Rashtrapati Bhawan, and Hawa Mahal. All monuments are open from sunrise to sunset. Chandani Chowk (Closed on Sundays). Taj Mahal is closed on Fridays\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 07:20:06','2025-11-15 07:20:06',NULL,54),(189,'{\"time\":1763191378723,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"A0oMZSkWPn\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 9:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763191378723,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"O5WzTNTBuN\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Wake up early in the morning to witness the breathtaking beauty of the royal magnificence of the Taj Mahal, a monument so captivating that you won\'t be able to take your eyes off it. At sunrise, as the first rays of dawn kiss the white marble, the Taj Mahal awakens in a golden glow, casting its reflection across the tranquil Yamuna River. This is the most enchanting time to witness the monument. Explore Mahal. Come back to your hotel and enjoy the comforting breakfast. After breakfast, check out of the hotel and start your exploration of a beautiful monument holding Indiaâ€™s ancient history that awaits you: â€œThe Agra Fort.â€ Standing on the banks of the River Yamuna, Agra Fort is also one of the most magnificent Mughal monuments and a UNESCO World Heritage site. Built in 1565 AD by the great Mughal emperor Akbar, the fort is made of red sandstone. Agra Fort stands as a symbol of architectural brilliance and a silent witness of centuries of Indiaâ€™s royal history, power, and love. Pause for a moment, and take a lunch break to refresh yourself and boost your energy. Afterwards, explore Agraâ€™s local market and enjoy Agra\'s famous â€œPetha.â€\"}},{\"id\":\"DE1NmU29NT\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"As your journey concludes, you return with a heart enriched by history, uplifted by spirituality, and filled with unforgettable moments from Indiaâ€™s most iconic destinations.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 07:22:58','2025-11-15 07:22:58',NULL,55),(190,'{\"time\":1763194642999,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"PkMjQGGdHg\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 8:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763194642999,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"h06mr0ylSb\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Check out from the Jaipur hotel after breakfast and enjoy a scenic drive to Agra (approx. 4-5 hrs. drive) via Fatehpur Sikri. Take a break for lunch and then visit Fatehpur Sikri, a UNESCO World Heritage Site built by Emperor Akbar in the 16th century. It was the capital of the Mughal Empire, built with red sandstone, and it is an architectural masterpiece that blends Persian, Indian, and Islamic styles. Walking through Fatehpur Sikri feels like stepping back in time, with its well-preserved palaces, courtyards, and gateways narrating stories of the Mughal eraâ€™s grandeur and vision. Depart for Agra and check in to your hotel and enjoy a comfortable overnight stay.&nbsp;\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:17:24','2025-11-15 08:17:24',NULL,55),(191,'{\"time\":1763194670415,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"x29EGCNqWs\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 7:&nbsp;</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763194670415,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"Ks7-plE-7f\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, meet your tour guide and explore the royal landmarks of the city, starting with Amber Fort located atop the Aravalli Hills. Built in 1592 by Raja Man Singh I, the fort is an architectural marvel blending Rajput and Mughal styles. Explore the mesmerizing beauty of Sheesh Mahal (Mirror Palace), Ganesh Pol, and the Diwan-i-Aam (Hall of Public Audience). The detailed mirror work and magnificent courtyards make it one of the most iconic forts of India. Now head towards City Palace, a grand complex that still serves as a residence of the royal family of Jaipur. Constructed by Maharaja Sawai Jai Singh II, the palace showcases a perfect blend of Rajput, Mughal, and European architecture. Towards the afternoon, take a quick lunch break and savor the flavors of Rajasthan. After regaining energy, move to your next location, Jantar Mantar, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Jantar Mantar is an astronomical observatory built in 1734 by Maharaja Jai Singh II, who was passionate about astronomy. The site contains 19 architectural instruments that can measure time, track celestial bodies, and predict eclipses, all with remarkable accuracy, centuries before modern equipment. Lastly, visit the Hawa Mahal, situated in the center of the city, Jaipurâ€™s most recognizable landmark. Built in 1799 by Maharaja Sawai Pratap Singh, this five-story pink sandstone structure has 953 small windows (jharokhas) adorned with intricate lattice work. Wind up your day with some shopping and exploring the vibrant market of Jaipur and enjoying a comfortable stay.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:17:51','2025-11-15 08:17:51',NULL,55),(192,'{\"time\":1763194697097,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"JgxEqyExM8\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 6:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763194697097,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"oS6nQSPaS2\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast head towards your private vehicle as your much-awaited journey begins. Depart from Delhi and take a scenic drive to Jaipur (approx. 5-6 hrs. drive). Reach Jaipur, the Pink City, by afternoon and check in to the hotel and relax after your journey. In the evening, visit the local market of Jaipur and then head towards Chokhi Dhani, where you enjoy the folk dance and music, camel rides, and wind up your day with a Rajasthani cultural dinner. Drive back to the hotel and enjoy your comfortable stay.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:18:18','2025-11-15 08:18:18',NULL,55),(193,'{\"time\":1763194721107,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"k87zEljZKC\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 5:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763194721107,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"MWlKy70OQE\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast head towards Amritsar Railway Station for your train to Delhi. Upon arrival in Delhi, meet the TrippyJiffy representative and check in at the hotel rest and enjoy that day on your own enjoying delhi\'s food and vibrant streets. Overnight stay at Delhi.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:18:42','2025-11-15 08:18:42',NULL,55),(194,'{\"time\":1763194746525,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"F8nzpgR6gG\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 4:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763194746525,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"-SY_NWsLn3\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After Breakfast at the hotel, start visit Golden Temple popular as Sir Harminder Sahib and the spiritual place of Sikh community Built by Guru Arjan Dev Ji. Then visit another historical site,&nbsp; Jallianwala Bagh: a historical garden located close to the Golden Temple. The place where a mass crowd of innocents was shot down on the command of British military officer Reginald Dyer. In the afternoon, explore the local markets, followed by a food experience at famous restaurants. Enjoy an overnight stay at the hotel.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:19:07','2025-11-15 08:19:07',NULL,55),(195,'{\"time\":1763194774909,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"VMXsfjSAHr\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 3:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763194774909,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"mMIHE3tOBp\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"&nbsp;After breakfast head towards your private vehicle as your much-awaited journey begins; depart from Delhi Railway Station and board a comfortable train to Amritsar. Arrive at Amritsar station, meet with TrippyJiffy\'s travel representative at the platform, and then transfer to the hotel. Later proceed to visit the Indo-Pakistan Border, or Wagah Border: a popular place located at Amritsar\'s outskirts where you can witness the flag ceremony. Overnight stay in Amritsar.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:19:35','2025-11-15 08:19:35',NULL,55),(196,'{\"time\":1763194797186,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"ace5l0bgT-\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 2:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763194797187,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"7mjnLRm0Kb\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, head towards your private vehicle and begin your journey, stepping back in time as you enter the beauty and chaos of Old Delhi. Explore the narrow streets of Chandni Chowk with a rickshaw ride and visit all the famous chaotic lanes like â€œParathe Wali Gali.â€ Experience a guided food walk tour and savor authentic flavors that define Delhiâ€™s culinary soul. Explore Jalebi Wala, Karimâ€™s, Al Jawahar, and Natraj Dahi Bhalla, and indulge as much as your heart (and stomach) can hold. Visit the Red Fort in Purani Dilli. Also, you can shop for beautiful Indian outfits and artifacts if time allows.&nbsp; Visit India Gate (the iconic war memorial dedicated to Indian soldiers) and Rashtrapati Bhavan (the majestic Presidential Residence outside view). Continue exploration where modernity blends with Mughal and colonial history by visiting Humayun\'s Tomb (the architectural inspiration behind the Taj Mahal). Qutub Minar (the worldâ€™s tallest brick minar, a UNESCO World Heritage site).&nbsp; As the day winds up, enjoy a comfortable stay at the hotel.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:19:58','2025-11-15 08:19:58',NULL,55),(197,'{\"time\":1763194822508,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"C6Edh6ojcR\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 1:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763194822508,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"RuowV2eNqZ\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Arrive in Delhi, meet TrippyJiffy\'s representative, and check in to your comfortable stay. Relax and enjoy the property. In the afternoon at 16:00 hrs depart for Dilli Haat, Delhi\'s iconic vibrant market filled with numerous options of Indian handicrafts and art collections.&nbsp; Witness some cultural events and enjoy your dinner at Dilli Haat, exploring Indian cuisines. Overnight stay in Delhi.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:20:23','2025-11-15 08:20:23',NULL,55),(198,'{\"time\":1763194856690,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"Evkh8Ldgbn\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Note:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763194856690,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"-z2VM7d9q8\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Driver passes are required at Red Fort, India Gate, Rashtrapati Bhawan, and Hawa Mahal. All monuments are open from sunrise to sunset. Chandani Chowk (Closed on Sundays). Taj Mahal is closed on Fridays\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:20:57','2025-11-15 08:20:57',NULL,55),(199,'{\"time\":1763195068016,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"8n8sHkCFNl\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 14:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763195068016,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"P_1qe4Sz05\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Wake up early in the morning to witness the breathtaking beauty of the royal magnificence of the Taj Mahal, a monument so captivating that you won\'t be able to take your eyes off it. At sunrise, as the first rays of dawn kiss the white marble, the Taj Mahal awakens in a golden glow, casting its reflection across the tranquil Yamuna River. This is the most enchanting time to witness the monument. Explore the Taj Mahal. Come back to your hotel and enjoy the comforting breakfast. After breakfast check out of the hotel, and start your exploration of a beautiful monument holding Indiaâ€™s ancient history that awaits you: â€œThe Agra Fort.â€ Standing on the banks of the River Yamuna, Agra Fort is also one of the most magnificent Mughal monuments and a UNESCO World Heritage site. Built in 1565 AD by the great Mughal emperor Akbar, the fort is made of red sandstone. Agra Fort stands as a symbol of architectural brilliance and a silent witness of centuries of Indiaâ€™s royal history, power, and love. Pause for a moment, and take a lunch break to refresh yourself and boost your energy. Explore Agraâ€™s local market and enjoy Agra\'s famous â€œPetha.â€\"}},{\"id\":\"mLuT7ng-G3\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"As your journey concludes, you return with a heart enriched by history, uplifted by spirituality, and filled with unforgettable moments from Indiaâ€™s most iconic destinations.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:24:29','2025-11-15 08:24:29',NULL,56),(200,'{\"time\":1763195092082,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"i3NmR1WBR_\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 13:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763195092082,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"FfdncozkOQ\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Check out from the Jaipur hotel after breakfast and enjoy a scenic drive to Agra (approx. 4-5 hrs. drive) via Fatehpur Sikri. Take a break for lunch and then visit Fatehpur Sikri, a UNESCO World Heritage Site built by Emperor Akbar in the 16th century. It was the capital of an empire built with red sandstone; itis an architectural masterpiece that blends Persian, Indian, and Islamic styles. Walking through Fatehpur Sikri feels like stepping back in time, with its well-preserved palaces, courtyards, and gateways narrating stories of the Mughal eraâ€™s grandeur and vision. Depart for Agra and check in to your hotel and enjoy a comfortable overnight stay.&nbsp;\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:24:53','2025-11-15 08:24:53',NULL,56),(201,'{\"time\":1763195117420,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"ooF8yJBRXj\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 12:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763195117420,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"2W_SQZKYjg\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After meeting your tour guide, explore the royal landmarks of the city, starting with Amber Fort located atop the Aravalli Hills. Built in 1592 by Raja Man Singh I, the fort is an architectural marvel blending Rajput and Mughal styles. Explore the mesmerizing beauty of Sheesh Mahal (Mirror Palace), Ganesh Pol, and the Diwan-i-Aam (Hall of Public Audience). The detailed mirror work and magnificent courtyards make it one of the most iconic forts of India. Now head towards City Palace, a grand complex that still serves as a residence of the royal family of Jaipur. Constructed by Maharaja Sawai Jai Singh II, the palace showcases a perfect blend of Rajput, Mughal, and European architecture. Towards the afternoon, take a quick lunch break and savor the flavors of Rajasthan. After regaining energy, move to your next location, Jantar Mantar, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Jantar Mantar is an astronomical observatory built in 1734 by Maharaja Jai Singh II, who was passionate about astronomy. The site contains 19 architectural instruments that can measure time, track celestial bodies, and predict eclipses, all with remarkable accuracy, centuries before modern equipment. Lastly, visit the Hawa Mahal, situated in the center of the city, Jaipurâ€™s most recognizable landmark. Built in 1799 by Maharaja Sawai Pratap Singh, this five-story pink sandstone structure has 953 small windows (jharokhas) adorned with intricate lattice work. Wind up your day with some shopping and exploring the vibrant market of Jaipur and enjoying a comfortable stay.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:25:18','2025-11-15 08:25:18',NULL,56),(202,'{\"time\":1763195142183,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"PuoCEwXuF3\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 11:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763195142183,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"js-JNqgFQ9\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast drive towards Jaipur, the capital city of Rajasthan state. Jaipur (3-4 hours) is also known as the â€œPink City.â€ Upon arrival, check-in to the hotel. Reach Jaipur the Pink City by afternoon and check in to the hotel and relax after your journey. In the evening visit the local market of Jaipur and then head towards Chokhi Dhani where you enjoy the folk dance and music, camel rides and wind up your day with a Rajasthani cultural dinner. Drive back to the hotel and enjoy your comfortable stay.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:25:43','2025-11-15 08:25:43',NULL,56),(203,'{\"time\":1763195166358,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"-leudvRsJV\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 10:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763195166359,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"-e9n32yzY-\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast drive to Pushkar (5-6 hours). On arrival, check in to the hotel. In the afternoon, visit the various temples and the sacred Pushkar Lake. Visit the only Temple of Lord Brahma. After this beautiful exploration, enjoy your comfortable overnight stay at the Pushkar hotel.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:26:07','2025-11-15 08:26:07',NULL,56),(204,'{\"time\":1763195194460,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"dwbKXB-WOh\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 9:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763195194460,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"ZUmHlcKiW4\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Start your day with a beautiful boat ride in Lake Pichola, admiring the beauty of Udaipur. Later, start your guided tour for that day; firstly, visit City Palace, built in the year 1725. Sahelion ki Bari, Jagdish Temple, the Indo-Aryan temple, Fateh Sagar Lake, and Bhartiya Lok Kala Mandir (Folk Art Museum). Overnight stay at Udaipur hotel.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:26:35','2025-11-15 08:26:35',NULL,56),(205,'{\"time\":1763195219178,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"-nW9XV7cJ4\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 8:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763195219178,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"DqOPS_4IqL\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Another day, another scenic drive after breakfast to Udaipur (5-6 hours), also known as the â€œCity of Lakes.â€ En route, stop at Ranakpur Jain Temple, this stunning 15th-century marble temple devoted to Deity Rishabhanatha, the founder of the Jain religion. Upon arrival, check in to the hotel and spend the rest of the day at leisure. Enjoy your comfortable overnight stay at the Udaipur hotel.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:27:00','2025-11-15 08:27:00',NULL,56),(206,'{\"time\":1763195293163,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"FwJ9ktbzR0\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 7:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763195293163,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"5oIosH2Usc\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Start another day of exploration after breakfast and drive to Jodhpur in your private vehicle (5-6 hours). Founded by Rajput chief Rao Jodha in 1459. Once the capital of the Marwar Kingdom, Jodhpur is also known as \\\"Blue City\\\" for its cluster of indigo-painted houses around the old town. Upon arrival, check in at the hotel and begin your half-day tour. Visit the majestic Mehrangarh Fort, and explore the intricately designed palaces like Moti Mahal, Phool Mahal &amp; Fort Museum. Later, visit Jaswant Thada, built in 1899, and the museum located in the Umaid public gardens. Overnight stay at a Jodhpur hotel.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:28:14','2025-11-15 08:28:14',NULL,56),(207,'{\"time\":1763195316333,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"aFDsZnCjho\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 6:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763195316333,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"kXDWn8C9Wu\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast enjoy a full guided tour of the Jaisalmer Fort, built in 1156 by Rawal Jaisal. &nbsp; Take a break for lunch and then move ahead towards another unique experience: drive to the Sand Dunes and enjoy a camel safari accompanied by a dance show while the sun is setting. Overnight stay at Jaisalmer.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:28:37','2025-11-15 08:28:37',NULL,56),(208,'{\"time\":1763195339816,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"KBNVEQ9ikC\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 5:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763195339816,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"GT6qP2463t\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After an early breakfast depart for Jaisalmer, \\\"The Golden City\\\" (5-6 hours); en route visit Pokharan. On arrival, check in at the hotel. Enjoy a comfortable overnight stay at a Jaisalmer hotel.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:29:00','2025-11-15 08:29:00',NULL,56),(209,'{\"time\":1763195368156,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"JDY_wqRp_c\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 4:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763195368156,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"bnAyHD_5rr\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast depart for the \\\"Desert Town,\\\" Bikaner (4-5 hours drive) On arrival, check in at the hotel. Later, to explore the beauty of Bikaner, visit the Junagarh Fort, built in 1593 AD. The fort has 37 palaces, pavilions, and temples showcasing Mughal, Gujarati, and Rajput architecture. Visit the temple of Karni Mata and Goddess Durga to experience the rare sight of thousands of rats being worshiped. Overnight stay at Bikaner hotel.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:29:29','2025-11-15 08:29:29',NULL,56),(210,'{\"time\":1763195392299,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"6Hxk2mUlFl\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 3:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763195392299,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"La2pWIvyZo\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast head towards your private vehicle as your much-awaited journey begins. Enjoy a scenic drive to Mandawa (6-7 hours). Arrive and check in at the hotel; we will head towards our half day tour in Mandawa, visit Gulab Rai Haveli, built in 1870. This haveli is also called \\\"Open Art Gallery\\\" and is famous for its intricate wall paintings and bold and expressive artwork depicting mythological scenes, royal portraits, and everyday life. Also visit Gaoenka Double Haveli, built in 1890 and known for its floral patterns and mirror work. Lastly, visit Bansidhar Newatia Haveli, built in 1921 and famous for its fusion of traditional and modern artistic imagination. Enjoy your comfortable overnight stay at Mandawa.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:29:53','2025-11-15 08:29:53',NULL,56),(211,'{\"time\":1763195416711,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"gaWQQ_Q_Cq\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 2:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763195416712,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"CMkoZol3FT\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, head towards your private vehicle and begin your journey, stepping back in time as you enter the beauty and chaos of Old Delhi. Explore the narrow streets of Chandni Chowk with a rickshaw ride and visit all the famous chaotic lanes like â€œParathe Wali Gali.â€ Experience a guided food walk tour and savor authentic flavors that define Delhiâ€™s culinary soul. Explore Jalebi Wala, Karimâ€™s, Al Jawahar, and Natraj Dahi Bhalla, and indulge as much as your heart (and stomach) can hold. Visit the Red Fort in Purani Dilli. Also, you can shop for beautiful Indian outfits and artifacts if time allows.&nbsp; Visit India Gate (the iconic war memorial dedicated to Indian soldiers) and Rashtrapati Bhavan (the majestic Presidential Residence outside view). Continue exploration where modernity blends with Mughal and colonial history by visiting Humayun\'s Tomb (the architectural inspiration behind the Taj Mahal). Qutub Minar (the worldâ€™s tallest brick minar, a UNESCO World Heritage site).&nbsp; As the day winds up, enjoy a comfortable stay at the hotel.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:30:17','2025-11-15 08:30:17',NULL,56),(212,'{\"time\":1763195443553,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"uYkbvGZZbe\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 1:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763195443554,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"lzVsmQOHvZ\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Arrive in Delhi, meet TrippyJiffy\'s representative, and check in to your comfortable stay. Relax and enjoy the property. In the afternoon at 16:00 hrs depart for Dilli Haat, Delhi\'s iconic vibrant market filled with numerous options of Indian handicrafts and art collections.&nbsp; Witness some cultural events and enjoy your dinner at Dilli Haat, exploring Indian cuisines. Overnight stay in Delhi.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:30:44','2025-11-15 08:30:44',NULL,56),(213,'{\"time\":1763195479493,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"42QpvVrlCg\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Note:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763195479493,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"heXJrBfBmE\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Driver passes are required at Red Fort, India Gate, Rashtrapati Bhawan, Hawa Mahal. All monuments are open from sunrise to sunset. Chandani Chowk (Closed on Sundays). Taj Mahal is closed on Fridays\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 08:31:20','2025-11-15 08:31:20',NULL,56),(214,'{\"time\":1763206829082,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"9D7vDDTd4I\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 14:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763206829082,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"_0tnOT-Hr8\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Wake up early in the morning to witness the breathtaking beauty of the royal magnificence of the Taj Mahal, a monument so captivating that you won\'t be able to take your eyes off it. At sunrise, as the first rays of dawn kiss the white marble, the Taj Mahal awakens in a golden glow, casting its reflection across the tranquil Yamuna River. This is the most enchanting time to witness the monument. Explore the Taj Mahal. Come back to your hotel and enjoy the comforting breakfast. After breakfast, check out of the hotel and start your exploration of a beautiful monument holding Indiaâ€™s ancient history that awaits you: â€œThe Agra Fort.â€ Standing on the banks of the River Yamuna, Agra Fort is also one of the most magnificent Mughal monuments and a UNESCO World Heritage site. Built in 1565 AD by the great Mughal emperor Akbar, the fort is made of red sandstone. Agra Fort stands as a symbol of architectural brilliance and a silent witness of centuries of Indiaâ€™s royal history, power, and love. Pause for a moment, and take a lunch break to refresh yourself and boost your energy. Afterwards, explore Agraâ€™s local market and enjoy Agra\'s famous â€œPetha.â€\"}},{\"id\":\"v-lvkm7Nsy\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"As your journey concludes, you return with a heart enriched by history, uplifted by spirituality, and filled with unforgettable moments from Indiaâ€™s most iconic destinations.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 11:40:29','2025-11-15 11:40:29',NULL,57),(215,'{\"time\":1763206853702,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"PqhaV8Npnn\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 13:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763206853702,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"ltEpiyDync\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Check out from the Jaipur hotel after breakfast and enjoy a scenic drive to Agra (approx. 4-5 hrs. drive) via Fatehpur Sikri. Take a break for lunch and then visit Fatehpur Sikri, a UNESCO World Heritage Site built by Emperor Akbar in the 16th century. It was the capital of the Mughal Empire, built with red sandstone, and it is an architectural masterpiece that blends Persian, Indian, and Islamic styles. Walking through Fatehpur Sikri feels like stepping back in time, with its well-preserved palaces, courtyards, and gateways narrating stories of the Mughal eraâ€™s grandeur and vision. Depart for Agra and check in to your hotel and enjoy a comfortable overnight stay.&nbsp;\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 11:40:54','2025-11-15 11:40:54',NULL,57),(216,'{\"time\":1763206882824,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"_G1zhMooNx\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 12:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763206882824,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"7zs1t5ust-\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After Breakfast meet your tour guide and explore the Royal Landmarks of the city starting with Amber Fort located atop of the Aravalli Hills. Built in 1592 by Raja Man Singh I, the fort is an architectural marvel blending Rajput and Mughal styles. Explore the mesmerizing beauty of&nbsp; Sheesh Mahal (Mirror Palace), Ganesh Pol, and the Diwan-i-Aam (Hall of Public Audience). The detailed mirror work and magnificent courtyards makes it one of the most iconic forts of India. Now head towards City Palace, a grand complex which still serves as a residence of the royal family of Jaipur. Constructed by Maharaja Sawai Jai Singh II, the palace showcases a perfect blend of Rajput, Mughal, and European architecture.Towards the afternoon take a quick lunch break and savour the flavours of Rajasthan. After regaining energy, move to your next location, Jantar Mantar, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Jantar Mantar is an astronomical observatory built in 1734 by Maharaja Jai Singh II, who was passionate about astronomy. The site contains 19 architectural instruments that can measure time, track celestial bodies, and predict eclipses, all with remarkable accuracy, centuries before modern equipment. Lastly, visit the Hawa Mahal, situated in the center of the city, Jaipurâ€™s most recognizable landmark. Built in 1799 by Maharaja Sawai Pratap Singh, this five-story pink sandstone structure has 953 small windows (jharokhas) adorned with intricate lattice work. Wind up your day with some shopping and exploring the vibrant market of Jaipur and enjoying a comfortable stay.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 11:41:23','2025-11-15 11:41:23',NULL,57),(217,'{\"time\":1763206909708,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"U2FepJHNBJ\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 11:&nbsp;</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763206909708,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"6PjePlSVS-\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast drive towards Jaipur, the capital city of Rajasthan state. Jaipur (3-4 hours) is also known as the â€œPink City.â€ Upon arrival, check in to the hotel. Reach Jaipur, the Pink City, by afternoon and check in to the hotel and relax after your journey. In the evening, visit the local market of Jaipur and then head towards Chokhi Dhani, where you enjoy the folk dance and music, camel rides, and wind up your day with a Rajasthani cultural dinner. Drive back to the hotel and enjoy your comfortable stay.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 11:41:50','2025-11-15 11:41:50',NULL,57),(218,'{\"time\":1763206938272,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"l6Dwj6p9nr\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 10:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763206938272,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"Sbt3ZevtbI\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast drive to Pushkar (5-6 hours). On arrival, check in to the hotel. In the afternoon, visit the various temples and the sacred Pushkar Lake. Visit the only Temple of Lord Brahma. After this beautiful exploration, enjoy your comfortable overnight stay at the Pushkar hotel.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 11:42:19','2025-11-15 11:42:19',NULL,57),(219,'{\"time\":1763206963762,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"DVv0XAV84a\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 9:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763206963762,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"wX28yPwg6H\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Start your day with a beautiful boat ride in Lake Pichola, admiring the beauty of Udaipur. Later, start your guided tour for that day; firstly, visit City Palace, built in the year 1725. Sahelion ki Bari, Jagdish Temple, the Indo-Aryan temple, Fateh Sagar Lake, and Bhartiya Lok Kala Mandir (Folk Art Museum). Overnight stay at Udaipur hotel.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 11:42:44','2025-11-15 11:42:44',NULL,57),(220,'{\"time\":1763206985910,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"rgZ9M7ZNC8\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 8:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763206985910,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"ViM2xv859a\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Another day, another scenic drive after breakfast to Udaipur (5-6 hours), also known as the â€œCity of Lakes.â€ En route, stop at Ranakpur Jain Temple, this stunning 15th-century marble temple devoted to Deity Rishabhanatha, the founder of the Jain religion. Upon arrival, check in to the hotel and spend the rest of the day at leisure. Enjoy your comfortable overnight stay at the Udaipur hotel.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 11:43:06','2025-11-15 11:43:06',NULL,57),(221,'{\"time\":1763207014770,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"Kf6mDtRbvy\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 7:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763207014770,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"U9NIsTRXAF\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Start another day of exploration after breakfast and drive to Jodhpur in your private vehicle (5-6 hours). Jodhpur was founded by Rajput chief Rao Jodha in 1459. Once the capital of the Marwar Kingdom, Jodhpur is also known as the \\\"Blue City\\\" for its cluster of indigo painted houses around the old town. Upon arrival check in at the hotel and begin your half day tour. Visit the majestic Mehrangarh Fort, explore the intricately designed palaces like Moti Mahal, Phool Mahal &amp; Fort Museum. Later visit Jaswant Thada built in 1899 and the Museum located in the Umaid public gardens. Overnight stay at Jodhpur hotel.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 11:43:35','2025-11-15 11:43:35',NULL,57),(222,'{\"time\":1763207047882,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"RufdNliDg6\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 6:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763207047882,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"tYpu3OfXd7\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast enjoy a full guided tour of Jaisalmer; visit the Jaisalmer Fort built in 1156 by Rawal Jaisal. Take a break for lunch and then move ahead towards another unique experience: drive to the Sand Dunes and enjoy a camel safari accompanied by a cultural dance show while the sun is setting. Overnight stay at Jaisalmer.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 11:44:08','2025-11-15 11:44:08',NULL,57),(223,'{\"time\":1763207087911,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"k50gbpm_eI\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 5:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763207087911,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"Sd7B15Uhez\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After an early breakfast, depart for Jaisalmer, \\\"The Golden City\\\" (5-6 hours); en route, visit Pokharan. On arrival, check in at the hotel. Enjoy a comfortable overnight stay at a Jaisalmer hotel.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 11:44:48','2025-11-15 11:44:48',NULL,57),(224,'{\"time\":1763207125305,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"ynBwRRVJvU\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 4:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763207125305,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"KB-4i4ba0w\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast depart for the \\\"Desert Town,\\\" Bikaner (4-5 hours drive) On arrival, check in at the hotel. Later, to explore the beauty of Bikaner, visit the Junagarh Fort, built in 1593 AD. The fort has 37 palaces, pavilions, and temples showcasing Mughal, Gujarati, and Rajput architecture. Visit the temple of Karni Mata and Goddess Durga to experience the rare sight of thousands of rats being worshiped. Overnight stay at Bikaner hotel.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 11:45:26','2025-11-15 11:45:26',NULL,57),(225,'{\"time\":1763207149483,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"9eCuEfiChO\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 3:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763207149483,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"oLvjDPXB1W\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast head towards your private vehicle as your much-awaited journey begins. Enjoy a scenic drive to Mandawa (6-7 hours). Arrive and check in at the hotel. We will head towards our half-day tour in Mandawa and visit Gulab Rai Haveli, built in 1870. This haveli is also called \\\"Open Art Gallery of Mandawa\\\" and is famous for its intricate wall paintings and bold and expressive artwork depicting mythological scenes, royal portraits, and everyday life. Also visit Gaoenka Double Haveli, built in 1890 and known for its floral patterns and mirror work. Lastly visit Bansidhar Newatia Haveli Built in 1921, it is famous for its fusion of traditional and modern artistic imagination. Enjoy your comfortable overnight stay at Mandawa.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 11:45:50','2025-11-15 11:45:50',NULL,57),(226,'{\"time\":1763207173301,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"J0EsaAL7pR\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 2:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763207173302,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"BoAjNmtFfb\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, head towards your private vehicle and begin your journey, stepping back in time as you enter the beauty and chaos of Old Delhi. Explore the narrow streets of Chandni Chowk with a rickshaw ride and visit all the famous chaotic lanes like â€œParathe Wali Gali.â€ Experience a guided food walk tour and savor the authentic flavors that define Delhiâ€™s culinary soul. Explore Jalebi Wala, Karimâ€™s, Al Jawahar, and Natraj Dahi Bhalla and indulge as much as your heart (and stomach) can hold. Visit the Red Fort in Purani Dilli. Also, you can shop for beautiful Indian outfits and artifacts if time allows.&nbsp; Visit India Gate (the iconic war memorial dedicated to Indian soldiers) and Rashtrapati Bhavan (the majestic Presidential Residence outside view). Continue exploration where modernity blends with Mughal and colonial history by visiting Humayun\'s Tomb (the architectural inspiration behind the Taj&nbsp; Qutub Minar (the worldâ€™s tallest brick minar, a UNESCO World Heritage site)).&nbsp; As the day winds up, enjoy a comfortable stay at the hotel.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 11:46:14','2025-11-15 11:46:14',NULL,57),(227,'{\"time\":1763207196545,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"IHwlYfWbmE\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 1:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763207196546,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"--LIKZWfiZ\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Arrive in Delhi, meet TrippyJiffy\'s representative, and check in to your comfortable stay. Relax and enjoy the property. In the afternoon at 16:00 hrs depart for Dilli Haat, Delhi\'s iconic vibrant market filled with numerous options of Indian handicrafts and art collections.&nbsp; Witness some cultural events and enjoy your dinner at Dilli Haat, exploring Indian cuisines. Overnight stay in Delhi.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 11:46:37','2025-11-15 11:46:37',NULL,57),(228,'{\"time\":1763207230947,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"yeIbc4JaOq\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Note:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763207230948,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"KSR0ZQvm41\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Driver passes are required at Red Fort, India Gate, Rashtrapati Bhawan, and Hawa Mahal. All monuments are open from sunrise to sunset. Chandani Chowk (Closed on Sundays). Taj Mahal is closed on Fridays\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 11:47:11','2025-11-15 11:47:11',NULL,57),(229,'{\"time\":1763207547654,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"CWVx34a9Hg\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 3:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763207547654,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"9_fEo7aN1F\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, check out and head towards Jaisalmer airport/railway station in your private vehicle. With beautiful memories, as this desert trail has it all for you. Take home the warmth of the desert, the colors of Rajasthan, and memories that last forever.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 11:52:28','2025-11-15 11:52:28',NULL,58),(230,'{\"time\":1763207572857,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"6avN1_CArG\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 2:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763207572857,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"UaQtMGlaLs\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast visit Jaisalmer Fort, popular as the Golden Fort of Rajasthan; Gadisar Lake, a man-made artificial lake surrounded by various temples; and Patwon Ki Haveli, the oldest haveli of Jaisalmer, which represents a beautiful artwork. Salim Singh Ki Haveli is an art of marvelous architecture, located at a serene point. Lastly, visit Rajkumari Ratnavati Girls School: a fine example of extraordinary school architecture, which is quite different and attractive. This school is specially built up for the girls belonging to poor families of Jaisalmer. In the evening enjoy your comfortable stay at Jaisalmer.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 11:52:53','2025-11-15 11:52:53',NULL,58),(231,'{\"time\":1763207596310,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"4R7HXKBcFV\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 1:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763207596311,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"4FDWOZE_yr\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Arrive at Jaisalmer airport/railway station, and then meet your TrippyJiffy\'s representative, who will assist you with check-in at the hotel. Head towards Pokhran (2-3 hours) and visit Pokhran sightseeing points like Pokhran Fort and Gandhi Sagar Lake. In the evening, head towards another unique experience: drive to Sand Dunes and enjoy a camel safari accompanied by a cultural dance show while the sun is setting, followed by a gala dinner. Overnight stay at Jaisalmer.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 11:53:17','2025-11-15 11:53:17',NULL,58),(232,'{\"time\":1763208437499,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"pYR4byuwqV\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 4:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763208437499,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"a51xe10ikg\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, check out of the hotel and head towards your private vehicle for your return trip to Delhi Airport/Railway Station with a bundle full of memories. Soaked in a perfect getaway of shimmering lakes, majestic palaces, and timeless charms.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 12:07:18','2025-11-15 12:07:18',NULL,59),(233,'{\"time\":1763208467817,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"dmTXNBMrCu\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 3:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763208467817,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"1ZcC1_E222\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast head to Mount Abu enjoy the scenic drive of 2-3 hours. Check in at the hotel and then enjoy another day of sightseeing. Visit the famous Dilwara Temples. It\'s a group of five Jain temples built between the 11th and 13th centuries. It\'s famous for the magnificent beauty of its marble carvings, considered amongst the finest in India. The temple includes Vimal Vasahi, Luna Vasahi, Pittalhar, Parshvanath, and Mahavir Swami. The craftsmanship is so intricate that the marble appears almost transparent in parts. Next in line is the Nakki Lake. Considered India\'s first man-made lake in ancient times, this spot is famous for photography, as it is very scenic. Lastly, before sunset, visit the Sunset Point, one of the most popular places in Mount Abu. The changing colors of the sky give a beautiful panoramic scene. Enjoy your night at your comfortable stay in Mount Abu.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 12:07:48','2025-11-15 12:07:48',NULL,59),(234,'{\"time\":1763208495413,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"xv2_iL6aLK\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 2:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763208495413,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"ba_z8lyeA6\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, start your beautiful journey of sightseeing in Udaipur. Visit City Palace, built over 400 years starting with Maharana Udai Singh II. Offers stunning views of Lake Pichola and the Aravalli range. Sahelion Ki Bari Built by Maharana Sangram Singh II in the early 18th century. Jagdish Temple is a Hindu temple built by Maharana Jagat Singh I dedicated to Lord Vishnu as Jagannath. Fateh Sagar Lake was built in 1687 and reconstructed by Maharana Fateh Singh, also known as the â€œSecond Kashmirâ€ due to its blue waters and surrounding hills. Lastly, visit Bharatiya Lok Kala, a cultural institution dedicated to Rajasthani culture, founded by Padma Shri Devendra D. Bhatt in 1952.&nbsp; Enjoy a beautiful scenic boat ride in Lake Pichola overlooking a Pinterest-worthy landscape. Overnight stay at a Udaipur hotel.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 12:08:16','2025-11-15 12:08:16',NULL,59),(235,'{\"time\":1763208517751,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"1joHyYUEVc\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 1:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763208517751,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"1VIyv_TpAj\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Arrive early morning at Delhi airport/railway station. Board your private vehicle and enjoy the most scenic drive to Udaipur (10-11 hours). Check in at your comfortable stay at Udaipur and relax.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 12:08:38','2025-11-15 12:08:38',NULL,59),(236,'{\"time\":1763208734839,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"UMjX8B9mVn\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 7:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763208734839,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"G1Aa4DNBIG\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, drive to the Cochin airport or Ernakulam train station (1-2 hours) and take a drop at your desired location. As this trip comes to an end, wrap your heart in Keralaâ€™s beauty as your journey concludes. Hoping the magic of Kerala made your holiday truly special.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 12:12:15','2025-11-15 12:12:15',NULL,60),(237,'{\"time\":1763208757802,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"ClElprnjNx\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 6:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763208757802,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"WLha3x4y3v\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, take a drive to your next scenic location, which is giving you a shoutout. Lying in the lap of nature is Alleppey (4-5 hours), widely known as the â€˜Venice of the East.\\\" Arriving in this gorgeous backwater destination, you will be checked in to a lovely houseboat. After settling down in, you can go for a houseboat cruise and maneuver the narrow canals, enjoy the captivating beauty of the coconut groves, never-ending paddy fields, scenic coir villages, and much more; overnight stay will be in the houseboat. Cruise through Vembanad Lake on the houseboat till evening before the houseboat gets parked while you enjoy your night stay on the houseboat. Enjoy you Overnight stay in Alleppey.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 12:12:38','2025-11-15 12:12:38',NULL,60),(238,'{\"time\":1763208784382,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"g0tsnIpljj\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 5:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763208784383,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"Nm_YlCUfli\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast head towards your private vehicle and enjoy your drive to Thekkady (3-4 hours). After checking in at the hotel and enjoying your sightseeing, take a spice plantation tour. Take a walk along the streets, enjoying the aroma of cloves, nutmeg, pepper, cinnamon, and cardamom.&nbsp;\"}},{\"id\":\"4Ut8wWZwBy\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"In the evening, enjoy a boat ride in the stunning Periyar Lake with a beautiful Pinterest-worthy landscape. Boat safari on the Periyar Lake through the Periyar Tiger Reserve. Periyar Wildlife Sanctuary is home to a wide variety of animal species. Be they mammals, reptiles, birds, insects, or amphibians, the sanctuary has them all in abundance. On your boat cruise enjoy the wildlife encounters and catch those moments in your camera. Spot the animals flocking to the lake to quench their thirst. Later you will be guided back to the hotel for your overnight stay at Thekkady.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 12:13:05','2025-11-15 12:13:05',NULL,60),(239,'{\"time\":1763208811502,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"BDz04HUnKR\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 4:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763208811502,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"xY0Ka50-Ju\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Begin your day with a delicious breakfast and get ready for the Munnar excursion. Visit several tourist spots and destinations within the hill station and admire its alluring charm. Visit the beautiful tea gardens, giving you a breathtaking landscape, and enjoy a tea tasting session in the tea factory. Next to the Mattuppetty dam and Kundala lake, visitors have the opportunity to go boating. Next, visit the echo point, top station &amp; rose garden. Towards the second phase of the day, visit Eravikulam National Park, famous for the Nilgiri Thar. Enjoy your evening at your cozy stay in Munnar.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 12:13:32','2025-11-15 12:13:32',NULL,60),(240,'{\"time\":1763208837064,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"VTMAwqEzmp\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 3:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763208837064,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"lI8x2M4nJ2\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast head towards your private vehicle and enjoy your drive to Munnar (4-5 hours). â€œNature Loverâ€™s Paradise, called Munnar, is located around 1,800 m above sea level. The hill station of Munnar is among one of the most charming and romantic destinations in Kerala. Enjoy this stunning hill abode, as you will be checking in to the hotel overnight.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 12:13:57','2025-11-15 12:13:57',NULL,60),(241,'{\"time\":1763208864392,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"jIJ9R-TDUb\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 2:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763208864392,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"9vWRv7IuXN\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast proceed for a city tour, including the Chinese Fishing Net (colonial name Cheenawala), which is one of the unique primitive mechanisms in which a net is fixed to a pole on the shore. While fishing, the whole net is dropped into water by the crude mechanism using long bamboo poles. By the same mechanism the pole is lifted along with the catches.\"}},{\"id\":\"99fM1sP-_N\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Jew Town, Synagogue: The unique feature here is the unexpected and isolated Jewish community, whose origin dates back to AD 52. They are self-contained and have their own synagogue.&nbsp;\"}},{\"id\":\"R_66yGFI2q\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Santa Cruz Basilica: The Santa Cruz Cathedral Basilica is one of the oldest churches in Cochin. In 1503, the Portuguese commander Dom Afonso de Albuquerque defeated the king of Cochin and gave them permission to build a fort. This part of the city reflects an unusual blend of medieval Portugal.&nbsp;\"}},{\"id\":\"4OMWO4rHr9\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Bolgatty Palaceâ€”This palace was built by the Dutch in India, which is located on the island popularly known as Bolghatty Island in Cochin. This is one of the oldest heritage properties in India made by the Dutch, as well as an existing Dutch palace outside Holland.&nbsp;\"}},{\"id\":\"O7e-FV0XLk\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"In the evening Enjoy Kathakali Dance, Kathakali is a classical dance-drama of Kerala since the 17th century, and it belongs to Hindu mythology. Kathakali is a combination of literature, music, painting, acting, and dance. The extremely stylized gesture, the elaborate make-up, the mask, and the glorious costumes of these all-male dancers recreate an unmatched sense of pageantry. Enjoy your overnight stay at the hotel in Cochin.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 12:14:25','2025-11-15 12:14:25',NULL,60),(242,'{\"time\":1763208888304,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"MNmCli_wpr\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 1:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763208888304,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"z87Jdv156c\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Arrive in Cochin and meet with TrippyJiffy\'s representative in the hotel\'s waiting lounge. Check in at the hotel; our tour representative would discuss the tour plan with you. Later you can enjoy your comfortable stay in Cochin.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 12:14:49','2025-11-15 12:14:49',NULL,60),(243,'{\"time\":1763221397251,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"7mHXL_1LzM\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Note:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763221397251,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"O_t29velcO\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Synagogue- (Mon &amp; Fri Closed). Bolgatty Palace (Monday &amp; Friday Closed). Nilgiri Thar [Closed in Feb &amp; Mar]\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 15:43:18','2025-11-15 15:43:18',NULL,60),(244,'{\"time\":1763221461191,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"9aJ2PdR7dM\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 11:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763221461191,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"ztdVRsyTQV\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, check out and visit Shree Padmanabhaswamy Temple, a Hindu temple dedicated to Vishnu, in Thiruvananthapuram, the capital of the state of Kerala, India. It is one of the 108 Divya Desams dedicated to Lord Vishnu. It is widely considered as the world\'s richest Hindu temple. Then head towards Trivandrum airport, where your journey through Trivandrum comes to an end. Take home the serenity of its temples, the charm of its beaches, and the richness of its cultural heritageâ€”memories that stay long after the trip is over.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 15:44:22','2025-11-15 15:44:22',NULL,61),(245,'{\"time\":1763221484461,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"p4nmCG8BK4\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 10:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763221484461,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"FOqqKWNEMq\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Breakfast at hotel. Optional - Abhyangam Swedanam (general body massage with steam). Day at leisure to relax and rejuvenate on pristine Kovalam Beach. Overnight is at the hotel in Kovalam.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 15:44:45','2025-11-15 15:44:45',NULL,61),(246,'{\"time\":1763221507542,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"FWbG_mLbYi\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 9:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763221507543,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"r3zIH_jpQP\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, check out and drive to Kovalam (5-6 hours). Check in at the hotel. Spend your day at your leisure and visit the famous Kovalam Beach. Kovalam is best known for its beaches and Ayurveda resorts. Overnight is at the hotel in Kovalam.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 15:45:08','2025-11-15 15:45:08',NULL,61),(247,'{\"time\":1763221539372,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"urqmwK2S_b\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 8:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763221539372,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"rfkqDMmweQ\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, spend your day enjoying the scenic beaches of Mararikulam. Marari beaches are safe for swimming. You can also go on a tour through the neighboring villages. Stroll around or cycle and observe the slow pace of life in the village. Watching the fisherfolk engaged in their daily chores is an interesting sight. Talk to local fishermen, and they may well give you a ride on their boats if they find it safe. Spend your day at your leisure admiring the beauty of Mararikulam with an overnight stay.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 15:45:40','2025-11-15 15:45:40',NULL,61),(248,'{\"time\":1763221578838,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"Ho8iYdTYwi\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 7:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763221578838,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"J5Ws42xIH_\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Wake up to a beautiful morning in the lap of nature. Enjoy a scenic breakfast at the houseboat. Check out and head towards Mararikulam; enjoy the scenic drive (1 hour). On arrival, check in at the hotel, and enjoy your comfortable stay at Mararikulam.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 15:46:20','2025-11-15 15:46:20',NULL,61),(249,'{\"time\":1763221612989,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"_DEc0rczcg\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 6:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763221612990,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"L14THyE5bP\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, take a drive to your next scenic location, which is giving you a shoutout. Lying in the lap of nature is Alleppey (4-5 hours), widely known as the â€˜Venice of the East.\\\" Arriving in this gorgeous backwater destination, you will be checked in to a lovely houseboat. After settling down in, you can go for a houseboat cruise and maneuver the narrow canals, enjoy the captivating beauty of the coconut groves, never-ending paddy fields, scenic coir villages, and much more; overnight stay will be in the houseboat. Cruise through Vembanad Lake on the houseboat till evening before the houseboat gets parked while you enjoy your night stay on the houseboat. Enjoy your overnight stay in Alleppey.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 15:46:54','2025-11-15 15:46:54',NULL,61),(250,'{\"time\":1763221640953,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"g-0EWh3ST1\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 5:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763221640954,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"m6AlDwuUqd\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast head towards your private vehicle and enjoy your drive to Thekkady (3-4 hours). After Check in at the hotel and enjoy your sightseeing Take a spice plantation tour. Take a walk along the streets, enjoying the aroma of cloves, nutmeg, pepper, cinnamon, and cardamom.&nbsp;\"}},{\"id\":\"Brq4WOglfF\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"In the evening, enjoy a boat ride in the stunning Periyar Lake with a beautiful Pinterest-worthy landscape. Boat safari on the Periyar Lake through the Periyar Tiger Reserve. Periyar Wildlife Sanctuary is home to a wide variety of animal species. Be they mammals, reptiles, birds, insects, or amphibians, the sanctuary has it all in abundance. On your boat cruise, enjoy the wildlife encounters and catch those moments with your camera. Spot the animals flocking to the lake to quench their thirst. Later you will be guided back to the hotel for your overnight stay at Thekkady.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 15:47:22','2025-11-15 15:47:22',NULL,61),(251,'{\"time\":1763221666038,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"q2lm85pt8Q\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 4:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763221666039,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"Xr6c0fRm-2\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Begin your day with a delicious breakfast and get ready for the Munnar excursion. Visit several tourist spots and destinations within the hill station and admire its alluring charm. Visit the beautiful tea gardens, giving you a breathtaking landscape, and enjoy a tea tasting session in &nbsp; Next to the Mattuppetty dam and Kundala lake, visitors have the opportunity to go boating. Next, visit the echo point, top station &amp; rose garden. Towards the second phase of the day, visit Eravikulam National Park, famous for the Nilgiri Thar. Enjoy your evening at your cozy stay in Munnar.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 15:47:47','2025-11-15 15:47:47',NULL,61),(252,'{\"time\":1763221695546,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"JMwTeSVPLG\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 3:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763221695546,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"riuw0UrxPi\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast head towards your private vehicle and enjoy your drive to Munnar (4-5 hours). â€œNature Loverâ€™s Paradise,â€ called Munnar, is located around 1,800 m above sea level. The hill station of Munnar is among one of the most charming and romantic destinations in Kerala. Enjoy this stunning hill abode, as you will be checking in to the hotel overnight.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 15:48:16','2025-11-15 15:48:16',NULL,61),(253,'{\"time\":1763221725964,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"ULUOhRo9Bp\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 2:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763221725965,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"xbUQ3IrP6W\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast proceed for a tour including the Chinese Fishing Net (colonial name Cheenawala), which is one of the unique primitive mechanisms in which a net is fixed to a pole on the shore. While fishing, the whole net is dropped into water by the crude mechanism using long bamboo poles. By the same mechanism the pole is lifted along with the catches.\"}},{\"id\":\"MomqEm-DF2\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Jew Town, Synagogue: The unique feature here is the unexpected and isolated Jewish community, whose origin dates back to AD 52. They are self-contained and have their own synagogue.&nbsp;\"}},{\"id\":\"uiA2qOGQXy\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Santa Basilica: The Santa Cruz Cathedral Basilica is one of the oldest churches in Cochin. In 1503, the Portuguese commander Dom Afonso de Albuquerque defeated the king of Cochin and gave them permission to build a fort. This part of the city reflects an unusual blend of medieval Portugal.&nbsp;\"}},{\"id\":\"TG4wBSWsl7\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Bolgatty Palaceâ€”This palace, built by the Dutch in India, located on the island, popularly known as Bolghatty Island in Cochin: This is one of the oldest heritage property in India made by the Dutch, as well as existing Dutch palaces outside Holland.&nbsp;\"}},{\"id\":\"WcsSz6YmIs\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"In the evening, enjoy Kathakali Dance. Kathakali is a classical dance-drama of Kerala, since the 17th century, and it belongs to Hindu mythology, Kathakali is a combination of literature, music, painting, acting and dance. The extremely stylized gesture, the elaborate make-up, the mask and the glorious costumes of these all male-dancers, recreates an unmatched sense of pageantry. Enjoy your overnight stay hotel, Cochin.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 15:48:47','2025-11-15 15:48:47',NULL,61),(254,'{\"time\":1763221751182,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"uW7cZNln9j\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 1:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763221751182,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"mPjg0Tk0bP\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Arrival in Cochin, meet with TrippyJiffy\'s representative in the hotel waiting lounge. Check in at the hotel; our tour representative would discuss the tour plan and hand over the documents to you. Thank you for giving us the opportunity to serve you.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 15:49:12','2025-11-15 15:49:12',NULL,61),(255,'{\"time\":1763221783082,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"6ObvPmkHfT\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Note:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763221783082,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"qyrKe8MhRO\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Bolgatty Palace (Monday &amp; Friday Closed). Nilgiri Thar [Closed in Feb &amp; Mar]\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-15 15:49:43','2025-11-15 15:49:43',NULL,61),(256,'{\"time\":1763297867255,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"7TAhx5yFlx\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 8:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763297867256,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"iKQGggYQ4n\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast drive to Bangalore airport for your return flight. Hoping the magic of Karnataka made your holiday truly special.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-16 12:57:47','2025-11-16 12:57:47',NULL,62),(257,'{\"time\":1763297899275,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"HzgIS6FsaU\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 7:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763297899275,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"Iv4USef0xV\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, head to your private vehicle and begin your journey back to Bangalore (8-9 hours). Drive to Bangalore and enjoy your comfortable overnight stay in a Bangalore hotel.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-16 12:58:19','2025-11-16 12:58:19',NULL,62),(258,'{\"time\":1763297939601,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"6R6393lC-s\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 6:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763297939602,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"6-mrOEcrn7\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast enjoy a delightful toy train ride from Ooty to Conoor. This is a UNESCO World Heritage train, which offers a nostalgic glimpse of the colonial era. This train journey is a treat to the eyes as you witness the breathtaking views of the Nilgiri mountains alongside the charming tunnels and lush tea gardens. It will give a truly unforgettable experience. Head back to Ooty and enjoy your stay at the beautiful property.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-16 12:58:59','2025-11-16 12:58:59',NULL,62),(259,'{\"time\":1763297985128,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"WA5m_2MoOj\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 5:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763297985128,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"_-sy1efv8Q\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, check out from the hotel and start your journey on a panoramic route to Ooty (7-8 hours); en route, visit the famous Ooty Lake. Arrive and check in to your beautiful property with an overnight stay.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-16 12:59:45','2025-11-16 12:59:45',NULL,62),(260,'{\"time\":1763298019721,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"H8ZtxvMARx\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 4:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763298019721,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"NQYjboSCcU\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, start your delightful excursion to visit Chamundeshwari Temple: Perched atop Chamundi Hill, about 13 km from Mysore, this temple is dedicated to Goddess Chamundeshwari, the presiding deity of Mysore. Built in the 11th century and expanded by the Wodeyars of Mysore, it showcases classic Dravidian architecture with a striking seven-tier gopuram (tower).\"}},{\"id\":\"UYas5mnHbW\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Next visit St. Philomenaâ€™s Church: one of the tallest churches in Asia, built in 1936 in Neo-Gothic style inspired by Germanyâ€™s Cologne Cathedral.&nbsp;\"}},{\"id\":\"zSDq-mzbSN\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"In the second half of the day, visit Brindavan Gardens. Situated below the Krishna Raja Sagar (KRS) Dam, about 20 km from Mysore. Built in the 1930s by Sir Mirza Ismail, the then Dewan of Mysore, the gardens are world-famous for their symmetric design, musical fountains, and illuminated evening shows.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-16 13:00:19','2025-11-16 13:00:19',NULL,62),(261,'{\"time\":1763298053081,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"NguwtQnTvL\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 3:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763298053081,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"j_xRFj0DIC\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast, start your scenic drive to Mysore via Srirangapatna, a town located on an island formed by the River Cauvery, giving it natural strategic protection and scenic beauty. Srirangapatna served as the capital of the Kingdom of Mysore under Tipu Sultan, famously known as the â€œTiger of Mysore. Reach Mysore. Check in to your hotel and enjoy your comfortable stay.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-16 13:00:53','2025-11-16 13:00:53',NULL,62),(262,'{\"time\":1763298092638,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"EB5g2SX8MH\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 2:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763298092639,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"viQHXps8EJ\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Wake up to enjoy a lavish breakfast spread. After enjoying your breakfast, start your Bangalore exploration.\"}},{\"id\":\"PO-SYUhtIO\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Visit Lalbagh Botanical Garden: A historic 240-acre garden established in the 18th century by Hyder Ali and later expanded by Tipu Sultan. Home to over 1,000 species of plants, including rare tropical and subtropical varieties. The Glass House, inspired by Londonâ€™s Crystal Palace, hosts the famous biannual flower shows. It also features a 2-billion-year-old rock, one of the oldest formations on Earth. Next in line of exploration is Tipu Sultanâ€™s Summer Palace: a splendid example of Indo-Islamic architecture, built in the late 18th century. Served as the summer retreat of Tipu Sultan, the â€œTiger of Mysore.â€ It also houses a museum displaying artifacts and paintings from Tipu Sultanâ€™s era. Take a pause for lunch to regain energy and begin the next phase of exploration: visit Bull Temple (Dodda Basavana Gudi), dedicated to Nandi, the sacred bull and mount of Lord Shiva. It is famous for its monolithic Nandi statue, carved from a single granite rock, measuring about 4.5 meters high and 6.5 meters long. It was built during the Vijayanagara period in the 16th century. In the evening, visit Vidhan Soudha: an iconic landmark and the seat of Karnatakaâ€™s State Legislature. Built in 1956, it is a magnificent example of Neo-Dravidian architecture, featuring grand granite steps and an impressive central dome. The building glows beautifully when illuminated at night. Later you can enjoy your comfortable stay in Bangalore.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-16 13:01:32','2025-11-16 13:01:32',NULL,62),(263,'{\"time\":1763298118553,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"1XQJGVGWeA\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 1:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763298118553,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"Mqt63NxZUq\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Arrive in Bangalore and meet with TrippyJiffy\'s representative in the hotel\'s waiting lounge. Check in at the hotel; our tour representative would discuss the tour plan with you. Later you can enjoy your comfortable stay in Bangalore.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-16 13:01:58','2025-11-16 13:01:58',NULL,62),(264,'{\"time\":1763298437796,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"M4lQqUc9nE\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 3:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763298437796,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"53yU35-7rz\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Breakfast at the resort. Later, check out from the resort and head towards Delhi Airport/Railway Station (4-5 hours). As your Jim Corbett exploration comes to an end, take home the thrilling experience of a jungle safari and the serenity of nature memories that will stay etched in your heart forever.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-16 13:07:17','2025-11-16 13:07:17',NULL,63),(265,'{\"time\":1763298463352,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"azMbWH9Rl2\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 2:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763298463352,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"0iXtEhHqAb\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Morning and evening exclusive jungle safaris by Jeep. During free time, experience the in-house activities at your resort. Overnight stay in Jim Corbett.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-16 13:07:43','2025-11-16 13:07:43',NULL,63),(266,'{\"time\":1763298498578,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"4Gy5ObjDPV\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 1:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763298498578,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"M-i7IpKjHC\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Arrive at Delhi Airport/Railway Station and head towards your comfortable private vehicle for your picturesque journey to Jim Corbett (4-5 hours). By afternoon you will reach Corbett or Ramnagar ethnic village and transfer to your resort. Lunch will be served at the resort. The evening proceeds for an excursion tour of the Kosi River followed by a visit to Girija Devi Temple, one of the most revered shrines in the region. Dinner will be served at the resort. Overnight stay in Jim Corbett.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-16 13:08:18','2025-11-16 13:08:18',NULL,63),(267,'{\"time\":1763298687790,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"EpSgozPfZD\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 3:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763298687790,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"jHsuzoS5zD\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"After breakfast at the resort. Checkout and head towards Jaipur Airport/Railway station (2-3 hours) As your Ranthambore National Park exploration comes to an end take home the thrilling experience of jungle safari and the serenity of nature memories that will stay etched in your heart forever.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-16 13:11:27','2025-11-16 13:11:27',NULL,64),(268,'{\"time\":1763298727016,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"MeTVlQkzLA\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 2:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763298727016,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"GEKEEMl-lp\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Early morning, you will be picked up from your resort and then proceed for the wildlife jungle safari. Enjoy the water bodies, flora and fauna, various species, and nature-developed tracks. After the jungle safari, return to your resort. Enjoy a warm breakfast at the resort. Continue your journey with a visit to the majestic Ranthambore Fort perched high above the jungle excursion; you will visit an ancient Ganesha temple, which is built in the fort premises. Enjoy your evening and a comfortable overnight stay at the Ranthambore resort.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-16 13:12:07','2025-11-16 13:12:07',NULL,64),(269,'{\"time\":1763298754860,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"yRxpG6pcwe\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"<b>Day 1:</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','{\"time\":1763298754861,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"W4MX_HR90g\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Arrive early morning at Jaipur Airport/Railway Station and drive to Ranthambore National Park (2-3 hours) in your private vehicle. On arrival, meet your representative, who will brief you about your schedule and help you with the check-in process. In the evening embark on your safari and immerse yourself in the majestic richness of flora and fauna. Enjoy your comfortable overnight stay at the Ranthambore resort.\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.0-rc.7\"}','2025-11-16 13:12:35','2025-11-16 13:12:35',NULL,64);
